LG:
  - Lightweight GL
  - Leyun's GL

Renderable management hierarchy:

  GLRenderable  (abstract: SetVertexAttributes, Buffer, Draw)
  ├── GLCompositeRenderable                        [contains a list of child GLRenderable objects]
  ├── GLTransformedRenderable                      [wraps any GLRenderable with a model matrix]
  ├── GLRenderableDecorator                        [identity decorator wrapping a GLRenderable]
  └── GLSimpleRenderable  (abstract: adds GetVertexArray/Buffer, GetDimension/NVertex/Vertex)
      ├── GLSimpleRenderableDecorator              [identity decorator wrapping a GLSimpleRenderable]
      │   ├── GLColorDecorator                     (abstract: color-related decorators)
      │   │   ├── GLUniformColorDecorator          [applies one uniform color to the whole renderable]
      │   │   └── GLBufferedColorDecorator         (abstract: adds a per-vertex color buffer)
      │   │       └── GLRandomColorDecorator       [assigns random colors to vertices]
      │   └── GLTextureDecorator                   [binds texture to renderable]
      │       └── GLBufferedTextureDecorator       (abstract: adds a per-vertex texture coordinate buffer)
      │           ├── GLPlanarTextureDecorator     [generates planar UV from x-y coordinates]
      │           └── GLSphericalTextureDecorator  [generates spherical UV from θ-φ coordinates]
      └── GLBufferedGeometry  (abstract: owns VAO/VBO; adds Bind, SetUniforms, IssueBuffer, IssueDraw)
          └── GLBufferedGeometryD<D>               [template; D=2 or D=3; owns typed vertex list]
              ├── GLTriangle                       (D=3)
              ├── GLTriangleStrip                  (D=3)
              ├── GLSphere                         (D=3)
              ├── GLCuboid                         (D=3)
              ├── GLAxes                           (D=3)
              ├── GLRectangle                      (D=2)
              ├── GLCircle                         (D=2)
              ├── GLSmiley                         (D=2)
              ├── GLSierpinskiGasket               (D=2)
              ├── GLSierpinskiGasketChaos          (D=2)
              ├── GLKochSnowflake                  (D=2)
              ├── GLBarnsleyFern                   (D=2)
              └── GLMaze                           (D=2)

Memo on caveats:

* GLApplication::SaveScreen() reads from the front buffer, which may have already been consumed (invalidated) by the windowing system, potentially producing undefined or garbage output. For example, on Ubuntu 25.10 with double buffering enabled, this issue can occur on the first-frame capture of the Maze example. On the other hand, calling glReadBuffer() on the back buffer immediately after drawing objects can cause the windowing system to malfunction.
